 - **Mixed video** (e.g. Seedance hook, Omni body): this skill only boards the Omni part. The Seedance part comes from `parts/seedance-storyboard.md`; say so at the hand-off.
 
 ## Omni prompts (one per clip)
-- Format: `The camera <holds steady | pushes forward toward the subject | tilts down slightly toward the X> as she <one simple action>. She says in a <accent from bible §7, default "standard American"> accent: "<exact line>" Natural movement, natural audio.`
-- **Action and line are two sentences** (". She says…", not "and says…"): with "and says" Omni did the action first, then spoke.
+- Format: `The camera <holds steady | pushes forward toward the subject | tilts down slightly toward the X>. From the very first frame she is already talking while she <one simple action>; the action happens during her words, not before them. She speaks naturally and continuously in a <accent from bible §7, default "standard American"> accent, with no pause before or inside the line: "<exact line>" Natural movement, natural audio.`
+- **Talk and act at the same time (student rule, 2026-10-28).** The old two-sentence format ("…as she drops the tomatoes. She says: …") made Omni do the action first and talk after: up to 2.4 s of silence at the start of a clip, which the student called "terrible". The format above is **proven** (Julia row 2 remake: first word at 0.00 s on both test clips). Still Whisper-check the first clip of every video before running the rest.
+- **Face-to-close-up push-in = Start + End frame (proven, student: "fucking amazing", 2026-10-28).** When the original zooms from the face onto an action (squashing a tomato over the counter), don't board the close-up alone. Make two images: a **start frame** (medium shot, face to camera, mouth open mid-sentence, palm-up hand already holding the prop, action just starting) and an **end frame** (the tight close-up of the action, face out of frame). Put both in Flow's Frames mode Start/End slots (Omni 1.1 Flash, same price as start-only: 6 s 720p = 10 credits). Prompt: `The camera starts on her face, then slowly pushes in and tilts down to a tight close-up of her hand, ending on the close-up of <the result>. From the very first frame she is already talking while she <action>; the <action> happens during her words, not before them. She speaks naturally and continuously in a <accent> accent, with no pause before or inside the line, and keeps talking once her face leaves the frame: "<line>" Natural movement, natural audio.` Result: talking at 0.00 s, smooth push-in from face to the squash, voice continues over the close-up. Use this whenever a shot moves from her face to an object.
+- **The line names what is happening in that same clip (student rule, 2026-10-28).** Pouring orange juice → she talks about the orange juice, never the next ingredient. Never copy an original video's offset where the words run one step behind the action; re-split the script so each clip's words match its own action.
+- **Whole sentences per clip.** Never split a sentence across two clips ("Blend it all for a full minute until" / "smooth and well mixed"): the cut lands mid-sentence and sounds like an unnatural pause.
 - **Regional slang pulls the accent**: words like "chuck in", "the lot", "mate", "reckon" (Australian/British originals) made the character switch to an Australian accent. When the character's accent differs from the original creator's, swap those words for plain equivalents ("add in", "it all") and tell the student which words changed.
 - **Accent in every clip**, from the character bible (§7 Voice). No pronunciation or delivery notes.
 - **Minimal hand movement**: one simple action that continues what the still shows. No lifting things toward the lens, no handoffs, no extra gestures (they glitch). Clips re-animated off one still can repeat the same action.
 - Word budget: <9 words 4s · 9–15 6s · 17–25 8s · 27–35 10s; split long talking at sentence breaks (~30 words max).
 - **Hook**: no default push. Write an eye-catching action from the video (e.g. green liquid oozing from the syringe onto the forehead) and set the image's `note`: "Hook note: tailored to this video. Adjust the action until it grabs attention. Not every hook needs a push."
 
+- **List lines pause (2026-10-28, banana bread clip 2):** a line that lists ingredients ("peanut butter, two eggs, and a little baking powder") made Omni pause 1.3 s after each item, timed to the spooning. Add "she says the whole list in one quick, flowing breath, no pause between items" to any clip whose line is a list, and Whisper-check the gaps (>0.6 s inside a sentence = redo).
+- **Flow failures:** Omni sometimes returns "Failed" (refunded). Just resubmit the same clip; a failed knife/cutting prompt went through when simplified ("picks up a slice"). Trim any ad-lib Omni adds before the line (ffmpeg -ss to 0.15 s before the first scripted word).
+- **Every named item goes in on camera, on its word (student rule, 2026-10-28).** Banana bread: bananas went in with the peel on, and "two eggs" were already in the bowl, never cracked in. Plan a visible action for each ingredient she names (crack the eggs, pour the powder) and never put an item into a start/end frame before she names it. Write prop state explicitly ("bananas fully peeled, no peel at all").
